{"id": "DbLZq8zMSbN", "title": "Video by codingmermaid.ai", "description": "10 agentic AI concepts you need before 2027 \n\nPeople who’ve never written a single line of code have full mouth of agent loops and systems that make them 7 figures while they sleep. But here’s the knowledge that survives contact with production in 2027.\n\n1. Harness engineering — designing the environment your agent acts inside: the sandbox, the file system, the runtime surface.\n\n2. Loop engineering — deciding when the agent runs again, and when it stops.\n\n3. Context engineering — getting the right information into the window and keeping the wrong information out.\n\n4. Tool design — your agent is only as capable as the tools you hand it, and only as safe as their worst edge case.\n\n5. Memory architecture — what the agent remembers, for how long, and what it's allowed to forget.\n\n6. Orchestration patterns — one agent, a planner, or a swarm; each fails differently.\n\n7. Guardrails & permissions — what happens when the agent tries something it shouldn't.\n\n8. Evals for agents — you can't test a trajectory the way you test a function.\n\n9. Human-in-the-loop design — knowing which decisions never get delegated.\n\n10. Observability & tracing — when it breaks at step 14 of 30, you need to see step 14.\n\nMost people are stuck on 3 and 4. The gap between a demo and a system is 7 through 10. And that’s exactly what I can teach you if you lock-in throughout the rest of the year. Comment “POST” for my FREE guide!", "channel": "codingmermaid.ai", "uploader_id": "39643192594", "uploader": "Danica Simic", "timestamp": 1784901532, "like_count": 9899, "comment_count": 552, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.c